silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_01_what_is_a_witness_concrete_anchor_5#citekeyadamekherrlichstrecker1990joyofcats silm:hasLongDescription "The CitekeyAdamekHerrlichStrecker1990JoyOfCats is LocalWitnessKey is the fourth node in the chain. For the joc620 witness, the local citation key is AdamekHerrlichStrecker1990JoyOfCats — the BibLaTeX entry pointing at the Joy of Cats monograph (1990 Wiley, freely redistributed in 2004). The key is the stable identifier that the cite Kleisli arrow uses to track provenance through the encyclopedia. A different witness from the same source (e.g., JoC §11.3 on universal property) reuses the same citekey but a different line range and verbatim quote." .
